Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese title screen version logo palettes
Applies after 0005-port-hooks.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

The Japanese "Emerald" version logo uses colours from the nine title
palettes, which the Japanese ROM loads into the nine reserved OBJ palettes
(there is no separate version palette). tools/localize_japanese.py stages
those 288 bytes as emerald_version.gbapal, with the Japanese logo, only into
a tree with this patch (it looks for TITLE_VERSION_PAL_JAPANESE).

--- a/src/title_screen.c
+++ b/src/title_screen.c
@@ -667,7 +667,14 @@
         LoadCompressedSpriteSheet(&sSpriteSheet_EmeraldVersion[0]);
         LoadCompressedSpriteSheet(&sSpriteSheet_PressStart[0]);
         LoadCompressedSpriteSheet(&sPokemonLogoShineSpriteSheet[0]);
+#if GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_JAPANESE
+        // TITLE_VERSION_PAL_JAPANESE: the Japanese version logo uses colours of the
+        // nine title palettes, which the Japanese ROM loads into the nine reserved
+        // OBJ palettes; emerald_version.gbapal holds those nine.
+        LoadPalette(gTitleScreenEmeraldVersionPal, OBJ_PLTT_ID(0), 9 * PLTT_SIZE_4BPP);
+#else
         LoadPalette(gTitleScreenEmeraldVersionPal, OBJ_PLTT_ID(0), PLTT_SIZE_4BPP);
+#endif
         LoadSpritePalette(&sSpritePalette_PressStart[0]);
         gMain.state = 2;
         break;
